# Summary
Introduced: a state-mutating debug endpoint was added to the pre-admission local_debug_response path. The storage checkpoint/compaction routine itself is legitimate maintenance functionality, but exposing it through this unauthenticated bypass path creates an availability risk.
When ARGMIN_LOCAL_DEBUG_ENDPOINT is enabled, handle() dispatches /__argmin/debug/* requests before acquiring the request semaphore. This commit adds POST /__argmin/debug/metadata-checkpoint/record/<pg_id> to that bypass path. Unlike the existing metrics endpoint, the new endpoint performs synchronous storage work: it records a metadata command checkpoint and attempts log compaction for the requested PG. A local unauthenticated client can repeatedly invoke this endpoint to force disk/SQLite/RPC-heavy checkpoint and compaction work outside max_inflight_requests backpressure, potentially starving Tokio workers or the storage node and causing denial of service. The endpoint is disabled by default and the argmin-s3 binary restricts it to loopback listeners, which limits exploitability, but the new mutating operation is still exposed without authentication or admission control whenever the debug endpoint is enabled.

# Resolution
Fixed for production/release builds by the local-debug endpoint hardening commits:

- `45497afe` gates local debug route dispatch and helper code behind `cfg(any(test, feature = "local-debug-endpoints"))`, and rejects `ARGMIN_LOCAL_DEBUG_ENDPOINT=1` at startup unless the binary was compiled with that non-production support.
- `73a36bcd` makes `local-debug-endpoints` a debug/test-only feature by adding a release-build `compile_error!`, and updates UAT smoke handling so debug-hook smokes cannot be run against release or externally supplied binaries.

The metadata-checkpoint debug endpoint remains a deliberate debug/test diagnostic hook, but it is no longer a production or release-build path. Production default builds reject the environment variable before startup, and release builds cannot be produced with the debug endpoint feature.

