## Report
Validated the finding at commit 824c430176dd0ab6e2bb3a5fa73a6c093340469c. The HTTP handler checks state.config.local_debug_endpoint and calls local_debug_response at crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:687-696 before request admission is acquired at crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:710-715. The POST /__argmin/debug/metadata-checkpoint/record/<pg_id> branch in local_debug_response parses the pg_id and directly invokes storage_node_for_request().record_current_metadata_command_checkpoint_for_pg(pg_id) at crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:1037-1053, with no SigV4 or other authorization checks in that path. The called storage method at crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:4373-4424 records a metadata checkpoint and calls compact_metadata_command_log_for_checkpoint_record after success, confirming state-mutating maintenance work. Dynamic validation: the existing targeted test `cargo test -p server-http local_debug_metadata_checkpoint_record_endpoint_bypasses_request_admission -- --nocapture` passed, proving the endpoint is reachable even when request_slots=0. I added a temporary PoC test that creates a bucket to populate metadata, starts the real HTTP server with local_debug_endpoint=true and zero request admission slots, then sends an unauthenticated local HTTP POST. It returned HTTP/1.1 200 with `pg_id=0 scanned=1 recorded=1 ... compacted=1 compaction_deleted_entries=1`, proving the debug endpoint triggers checkpoint recording and compaction despite bypassing admission. Debugger validation with LLDB broke at `storage::cluster::StorageCluster::record_current_metadata_command_checkpoint_for_pg` and showed the stack `handle at serve.rs:688 -> local_debug_response at serve.rs:1053 -> record_current_metadata_command_checkpoint_for_pg at cluster.rs:4377`, confirming the pre-admission debug path reaches the mutating storage routine. Crash reproduction is not applicable because this is an availability/admission-control design flaw rather than a memory-safety crash. Valgrind was unavailable in the container and Rust ASan required nightly-only -Z flags, so those methods could not be used. Exposure limits were also confirmed in code: ARGMIN_LOCAL_DEBUG_ENDPOINT defaults false at crates/argmin-s3/src/config.rs:322-325 and the argmin-s3 binary requires a loopback listener when enabled at crates/argmin-s3/src/config.rs:444-460.

